Although i'm grateful for the lizard as a method of curing stoning, I
do agree that it seems a bit farfetched. Not to say that dragons and
magical spells are firmly in the realm of reality, but the fact that
this is a game based in a fantasy dungeon doesen't mean that things
like this should be written off as "magic." There are, perhaps, other
methods that could become a more acceptable solution to this problem.
Off the top of my head, perhaps (a)pplying an acid blob corpse or
something like that.

Of course, this sort of change, while perhaps more realistically
plausible than consuming a lizard corpse to turn one's flesh back from
stone, might change the very mechanics of the way one currently deals
with a cockatrice. Being as though acid blobs decay eventually, one
would have to be very conservative when approaching anything that could
stone you, be it chickatrice or cockatrice.

Personally, I believe the best all-around solution would be to patch in
a herb or potion of some sort, that counteracts the effects of becoming
petrified. A source of stoning resistance might be nice as well,
although that could make the game significantly easier.



